{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["And the word <b>שכבתך.</b> I have already explained it. And it is possible that שכבתך is from שכיבה (lying), for at the lying-down an emission occurs, and just as he said regarding a married woman לטמאה בה (to defile her), so he said regarding a beast." "<b>ובכל בהמה.</b> Female." "<b>ולפני בהמה.</b> Male." "<b>לרבעה.</b> Turn to the beast, for the woman is the one mounted, and this word is from the root אדבעה." "<b>תבל הוא.</b> The grammarians said that this word is from reduplication, like תמס יהלוך, and the tav is added. And they said that its meaning is like השחתה (corruption). And some say that also מבול is from it, and it is close to the root בלל (to mix) — 'the lip of all the earth.' And by this general rule Scripture prohibited every kind that a person could couple with: a married woman, a foreign woman, and one who cannot bear offspring, for a kind does not reproduce except from its own kind and with its own kind."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:46.419262765Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}